## Subagent models

- **Default: inherit.** Every subagent uses the same model as the parent chat. Pass `inherit` (or omit the model) on every spawn, for every subagent type. Never choose another model yourself, even for "cheap" or "fast" work like research, exploration, or browser tests.
- **User override.** If the user names a model for subagents, use exactly that model on every spawn until they say otherwise.
- **Reset.** If the user says to switch back, use the default, or use the same model as this chat, the override ends and subagents inherit again.
- **Before each spawn,** find the most recent model instruction in the conversation and follow it. If there is none, inherit.
- **Unavailable model.** If the requested model is not one you can use for subagents, do not substitute. Skip the spawn, say which model was unavailable, and list the available ones.

## Delegation

Spawn subagents for work that can run in parallel or that a skill says to delegate. Skills do not choose models; only this rule does.
